{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HCgjRTF3uikN6hcZw9Qbu","type":"tool_result","content":"16944:type PollarLoginOptions = {\ntype TxSignContent = TxSignResponse['content'];\ntype TxSubmitSignedBody = Exclude<NonNullable<paths['/tx/submit']['post']['requestBody']>['content']['application/json'], {\n    chain: 'SOLANA';\n}>;\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitBody = NonNullable<paths['/tx/build-sign-submit']['post']['requestBody']>['content']['application/json'];\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitResponse = paths['/tx/build-sign-submit']['post']['responses'][200]['content']['application/json'];\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitContent = TxBuildSignSubmitResponse['content'];\n/**\n * Discriminated union of every login the SDK understands. The built-ins\n * (`google`, `github`, `email`) are explicit members; any registered wallet\n * adapter is reached through the catch-all via `login({ provider: adapter.type })`.\n */\ntype PollarLoginOptions = {\n    provider: 'google';\n} | {\n    provider: 'github';\n} | {\n    provider: 'email';\n    email: string;\n} | ({\n    provider: string & {};\n} & Record<string, unknown>);\n/**\n * Curated, stable facade handed to every {@link PollarAuthProvider}. It exposes\n * only the primitives a login strategy needs - the shared backbone\n661:         * @description For custom login providers (Privy, Magic, …) that authenticate the user client-side and surface a Stellar wallet. Control is proven with the same SEP-10 counter-signed challenge (from /auth/wallet/challenge); Pollar needs nothing of the provider itself.\n799:         * @description DPoP-bound resume/validate + touch. Confirms the refresh-token family is still active, returns the same profile shape as login `data` (mail, names, avatar, providers), and records the return (last_used_at + UA/IP-hash). Does NOT rotate the refresh token or create a new family. A revoked/expired family returns 401 so the client can converge to a logged-out state.\n16273:    /** Stable id - matches `login({ provider: id })` and the server-side wallet provider. */\n16312: * The UI calls these methods to run the provider login; once they resolve, it\n16313: * triggers the normal `login({ provider })` so `connect()` runs and core does the\n16322:    /** Email login step 2: verify the OTP; resolves once the provider authenticates. */\n16324:    /** OAuth login; resolves once the provider authenticates. */\n16325:    loginWithOAuth(provider: 'google' | 'github'): Promise<void>;\n16328:     * this to auto-trigger `login({ provider })` when the provider authenticates\n16468: * Embedded-wallet login methods - the providers that map to an `internal` wallet.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"744e830a-1f76-4ce2-97b8-7e3bec158cf2","uuid":"43081d01-ed1e-45e4-9fe7-df02f8c02bef","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:43:20.648Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"16944:type PollarLoginOptions = {\ntype TxSignContent = TxSignResponse['content'];\ntype TxSubmitSignedBody = Exclude<NonNullable<paths['/tx/submit']['post']['requestBody']>['content']['application/json'], {\n    chain: 'SOLANA';\n}>;\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitBody = NonNullable<paths['/tx/build-sign-submit']['post']['requestBody']>['content']['application/json'];\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitResponse = paths['/tx/build-sign-submit']['post']['responses'][200]['content']['application/json'];\ntype TxBuildSignSubmitContent = TxBuildSignSubmitResponse['content'];\n/**\n * Discriminated union of every login the SDK understands. The built-ins\n * (`google`, `github`, `email`) are explicit members; any registered wallet\n * adapter is reached through the catch-all via `login({ provider: adapter.type })`.\n */\ntype PollarLoginOptions = {\n    provider: 'google';\n} | {\n    provider: 'github';\n} | {\n    provider: 'email';\n    email: string;\n} | ({\n    provider: string & {};\n} & Record<string, unknown>);\n/**\n * Curated, stable facade handed to every {@link PollarAuthProvider}. It exposes\n * only the primi