{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0196DGBzQfETZusgGftYNjej","type":"tool_result","content":"wallet networks. Use `RampChain.POLYGON` or `'POLYGON'` for a quote filter,\nroute asset or signer registration. Chain and network are separate fields;\nlowercase names, unknown chains and CAIP-2 identifiers are rejected. Adding\nanother chain requires a backend enum migration and an updated SDK contract.\nExact amount strings keep their precision and formatting.\n\nRegister a signer for each chain/encoding pair a leg may ask for with `registerRampSigningHandler(chain, encoding, async action => signedPayload)`, `STELLAR`/`xdr` included: core has no built-in ramp signer. In a Stellar signer, `assertRampStellarSigner(action, address)` refuses a transaction that does not spend from `address` (or a SEP-10 login that is not the anchor's challenge for it). Handlers must validate the payload and authorized wallet account, chain and network before returning a signed payload without broadcasting it. Polling never invokes signing.\n\nThe backend lists only the routes its configured rails, venues and bridges can run.\n\n---\n\n### Earn (yield vaults + lending)\n719:Establishes (omit `limit`) or removes (`limit: '0'`) a trustline for `{ code, issuer }`. Who pays is decided\n738:  buyAsset: 'USDC:GA5Z...',\n774:  asset: { code: asset.code, identifier: asset.identifier, chain: asset.chain },\n802:lowercase names, unknown chains and CAIP-2 identifiers are rejected. Adding\n# @pollar/react\n\nReact bindings for [Pollar](https://pollar.xyz) — drop-in authentication UI, transaction modals, and hooks for\nStellar and Solana applications.\n\n> **0.12.0** (requires `@pollar/core@^0.12.0`). `<RampWidget>` runs on the v3 ramps API: routes, quotes leg by\n> leg, the fields a quote asks for, the order's progress and its pending action; it signs a leg with the connected\n> Stellar or Solana wallet only when the leg was built for it. **Wallets the user holds**: the wallet button lets the\n> user pick co-signed or self-custody when the app leaves it to them, `<RecoveryModal>` manages passkeys, email,\n> devices and the recovery phrase (`recoveryLocked`, `openRecoveryModal()`), and `<CustodyMigrationModal>` moves a\n> custodial wallet to Turnkey after login. `<SendModal>` offers to create a Stellar account that does not exist.\n> Branding yields to the host stylesheet, with `--pollar-font-family` and `--pollar-font-family-mono`;\n373:| `<SwapModal>`                 | On-chain asset-to-asset swap: pick from/to assets and amount, quote across venues, execute (auto-trustline on the buy asset when needed); paste a custom buy token (code + issuer)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n377:| `<WalletBalanceModal>`        | Multichain wallet balances (Stellar, Polygon, Solana). A `<ChainSelect>` picks the network and the rows are filtered to it; shows that chain's address plus a refresh button, and each row's issuer with a copy action. An unreadable chain's balance renders as a dash, never as `0`. On Solana testnet each row offers a faucet hint — a devnet SOL faucet on the native row, Circle's USDC faucet on the USDC row |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"744e830a-1f76-4ce2-97b8-7e3bec158cf2","uuid":"c6b361ed-0f65-4682-9861-9dec2c3b311e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:43:43.854Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"wallet networks. Use `RampChain.POLYGON` or `'POLYGON'` for a quote filter,\nroute asset or signer registration. Chain and network are separate fields;\nlowercase names, unknown chains and CAIP-2 identifiers are rejected. Adding\nanother chain requires a backend enum migration and an updated SDK contract.\nExact amount strings keep their precision and formatting.\n\nRegister a signer for each chain/encoding pair a leg 