{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsvkw9FxbXSv2X7S1k4b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The app is upgraded from Pollar 0.10 to the current SDK, 0.12.0. `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, and the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. I could not test against the live API (no network or test credentials here), so the changes are checked against the 0.12 type declarations and the SDK's own source, not a live call.\n\n**What was broken and what I changed:**\n\n- **API version (`src/pollar.ts`):** `baseUrl` is now the origin `https://sdk.api.pollar.xyz`. The SDK appends `/v3` itself. The old `.../v1` value would have produced `.../v1/v3`.\n- **\"Add money\" (`src/ramp.ts`):** `getRampsQuote` no longer exists. The function now lists the ramp routes, keeps the ARS → USDC-on-Stellar ones, quotes each, and returns the lowest ARS-per-USDC rate (`amountIn / amountOut`). \"No route\" counts as no quote, as before.\n- **Trustline (`src/trust.ts`):** the `sponsored` flag was removed. Sponsorship is now on by default and set by the app's dashboard.\n- **KYC (`src/kyc.ts`):** added the new `'expired'` status, shown as \"Verification expired\".\n- **Balances (`src/balances.ts`):** a `null` balance (chain unreadable) now shows as \"unavailable\" instead of `NaN`.\n- `src/App.tsx` and `src/Wallet.tsx` needed no changes.\n\n**Things to check before the cutover:**\n\n- **Sponsorship:** the USDC trustline is only sponsored if the dashboard allows it. Otherwise the user pays the reserve.\n- **Stellar asset identifier:** I took the issuer address as the ramp asset `identifier`, based on the SDK's own code. A live test would confirm it.\n- **CORS:** 0.12 sends an `x-pollar-sdk` header, which the API must allow. The creator's site needs to be checked if it is on a different origin.\n- **No `UPGRADE.md`:** the package points to one, but it isn't in the npm tarball, so I worked from the README and the type declarations.\n\n`package.json` and `package-lock.json` are updated. `node_modules/` is now untracked, since the repo has no `.gitignore`. I did not add one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2589,"cache_read_input_tokens":94865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2589},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"744e830a-1f76-4ce2-97b8-7e3bec158cf2","uuid":"419c043a-b6f7-4f63-976d-8e7699731da9","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:44:38.645Z","request_id":"req_011CgsvkvyqX1E4UEbsXVMRA"}
